flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the check of the package compares
    accDescr: krankerl packages the commit in HEAD and leaves out what .nextcloudignore lists. scripts/check-package.sh takes the runtime files of the same commit, those in appinfo, css, img, js, l10n, lib and templates and CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE and README.md, and compares the package with them file by file. A file that the package lacks, a stray file, a changed file or a link fails the check with the list of the differences. A package that holds exactly these files, and its signature once it is signed, passes if its PHP and JavaScript parse, and otherwise fails with the file that doesn't. The release workflow checks the package again after signing.

    head["The commit<br>in HEAD"]
    krankerl["`krankerl packages it<br>*and leaves out*<br>*what it ignores*`"]
    package["The package"]
    runtime["Its runtime files:<br>appinfo · css · img<br>js · l10n · lib<br>templates<br>changelog, license<br>and README"]
    same{"The same files,<br>each with the same content?"}
    differences["❌ Fails with the list:<br>missing · stray · changed"]
    parse{"Does its PHP and<br>JavaScript parse?"}
    broken["❌ Fails with the file<br>that doesn't parse"]
    passed["✅ Passes, and again<br>after signing"]

    head --> krankerl --> package --> same
    head --> runtime --> same
    same -- "no" --> differences
    same -- "yes" --> parse
    parse -- "no" --> broken
    parse -- "yes" --> passed

    classDef source fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef refused fill:#c9302c1f,stroke:#c9302c,stroke-width:2px
    class head,runtime source
    class krankerl,package,same,parse check
    class passed done
    class differences,broken refused
